# Hooks Maintenance

**Role:** enforcement layer for policies owned elsewhere. Map, behaviors, and known limitations: [hooks/README.md](../hooks/README.md).

## After editing hooks

- Run `pnpm hooks:smoke` — requires a writable `.cursor/hooks-state/` (gitignored). It does **not** replace the project gate in [quality-gates.mdc](quality-gates.mdc)
- Update the Quick map row in [hooks/README.md](../hooks/README.md) when a script, event, matcher, or behavior changes

## Rules

- **Critical denies** — `commit-policy.mjs` and `gate-before-commit.mjs` keep `"failClosed": true` in `hooks.json`; a crashed guard must not silently allow `git commit`
- Hooks enforce a **regex subset** of `*-sot.mdc` editorial prose — do not migrate editorial rules into hooks, or hook internals into rules
- Shared path / lint helpers live in `.cursor/hooks/lib/` (`living-sot-doc.mjs` is a barrel over `living-sot-paths` / `living-sot-lints` / `living-sot-registry`). Register new living-doc checks in `LIVING_SOT_ENTRIES` rather than hand-rolling per-guard logic
- Smoke cases live under `.cursor/hooks/smoke/` (`harness.mjs`, `cases.mjs`, `sot-samples.mjs`); entrypoint remains `smoke-test.mjs`
- Policy text stays in [commit-policy.mdc](commit-policy.mdc) and [quality-gates.mdc](quality-gates.mdc) — hooks reference it, never redefine it
- Paths arriving from Cursor may be absolute — normalize against the workspace root before classifying (see `lib/track-path.mjs`)
